Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:57:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 24/35] minimize: hover preview for items in the overflow popup

Windows in the overflow popup had no preview, so the only way to tell
two of them apart was the truncated label. Their items now use the same
preview tooltip as the panel, with the overflow popup as the preview's
parent surface, and the preview opens to the right of the hovered item
(the positioner flips it left when there is no room).

preview_tooltip takes the parent surface and the side to open on; the
side's anchor, gravity and offset are a small tested function. While the
overflow popup is open only its own items start a preview and a live
capture. Closing the overflow popup, by the button or by the compositor,
also closes its preview and stops the capture. Previews stay off while a
window menu is open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
